      "writtenOn": "2026-11-20T09:16:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "postDescribesAssocs() only walks newConfiguration, and deriveNewConfiguration() removes every configuration that was already in the previous run. If the platform configuration is published in one scan and the board its records name is found in a later scan (the board is new, the platform is not), the platform is not in newConfiguration, so those records never get the association and nothing retries it until the platform is published again. The existing topology associations avoid this because topology.getAssocs() works from all known boards.\n\nCould this also re-evaluate platform records whose Board matches a newly added board (or reuse Topology), so the result does not depend on which scan finds each side first?",
      "revId": "47c4f2a6aec95ce12321f479c98b2e969c85c61f",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
